From 6ab779570422bfe658074575a7bff77b88f62569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:13:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mission progress moves to an ini, and marks on every route to
 a win

Bob asked for a universal file, and the ini is also the more robust store.
GameMaker's ini_* functions read and write the sandboxed save area as one
operation with no separate load step to get wrong, and ini_close() is what
commits the file - so a write cannot land somewhere the next read does not look.
settlers.ini, section [missions], one key per mission, so other settings can
move in later without disturbing this one.

Two ways the old version could fail silently, both now closed:

- The in-memory flags were sized from game_info_get_mission_count(). Had that
  ever been empty or not yet built the first time progress was asked about - and
  the very first thing that asks is the start screen, on frame one - the array
  would have been EMPTY AND CACHED THAT WAY for the session: every mission reads
  as not done and every attempt to record one is dropped. PROGRESS_MIN_SLOTS
  (64) floors the size so that is unreachable, and a write past the end extends
  the array rather than being refused, so an index the table does not know about
  is still stored.

- check_game_over returns immediately when game_over is already set, so it is
  reached exactly once, at the instant of victory. A game restored from a save
  written after the win - or any other route arriving with the result already
  decided - never got there. Interface.update now marks the mission at the point
  the result reaches the player as well. Marking is idempotent, so both paths
  running is fine and either alone is enough.

Also logs what it is doing: which mission is being started, where the ini lives,
how many completions were read back, and - as before - when a win carries no
mission index to record.

